    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I've attached the benchmark datasets for both architectures. The Llama-derivative has much lower inference costs and high throughput for standard NLP tasks, but we've noticed it struggles with the high-dimensional causal reasoning and multi-step logic chains that our proprietary engine handles natively. \n\nLooking at these numbers, can you give me an assessment of whether the switch is actually viable for our core reasoning workflows?",
